# Runner-fleet compose override layering (OMN-14027 C1).
#
# Newline-delimited list of compose override files that MUST be layered on top of
# docker-compose.runners.yml by every tool that recreates runner containers, so a
# deliberate non-default wiring survives auto-repair and rolls.
#
# Consumed by docker/runners/runner-monitor.sh (auto-bounce / offline-idle
# recreate). Paths are relative to the compose directory unless absolute.
# '#' starts a comment. A listed-but-missing file WARNs and is skipped; it never
# wedges auto-repair.
#
# WHY: before this list existed, auto-repair recreated containers from
# docker-compose.runners.yml alone and silently stripped canary wiring mid-soak,
# with no log line and no alert. See knowledge-base:runbooks/pypi-cache-egress-rollout.md
# ("Durability trap").
#
# The C1 PyPI canary entry was removed when that canary ended (its three
# runners were retired with the rest of the primary host's general pool,
# OMN-22898). A new canary override is listed here again while it lasts and
# removed when it ends, either because the rollout graduated to the fleet (the
# wiring then belongs in docker-compose.runners.yml itself) or was rolled back.

docker-compose.model-review-canary.yml
